  "caption_groups": [
    {
      "start": 0.852083,
      "end": 2.727083,
      "text": "In Europe, beavers were reduced to"
    },
    {
      "start": 2.740125,
      "end": 4.8364579999999995,
      "text": "fragmented populations across several"
    },
    {
      "start": 4.8625,
      "end": 6.711499,
      "text": "regions before conservation efforts"
    },
    {
      "start": 6.7375,
      "end": 8.404166,
      "text": "successfully helped them recover."
    },
    {
      "start": 10.144083,
      "end": 12.474832,
      "text": "Combined population numbers were estimated"
    },
    {
      "start": 12.500875,
      "end": 14.636291,
      "text": "at small totals for specific rivers and"
    },
    {
      "start": 14.662333,
      "end": 16.511291,
      "text": "basins located throughout Europe."
    },
    {
      "start": 17.812083,
      "end": 19.765249,
      "text": "Beavers live naturally in freshwater"
    },
    {
      "start": 19.79125,
      "end": 21.197540999999998,
      "text": "ecosystems such as rivers,"
    },
    {
      "start": 21.405833,
      "end": 23.489166,
      "text": "streams, lakes and ponds where they build"
    },
    {
      "start": 23.515208,
      "end": 23.996999000000002,
      "text": "dams."
    },
    {
      "start": 25.336083000000002,
      "end": 27.849124,
      "text": "The keystone species concept became popular"
    },
    {
      "start": 27.875166,
      "end": 30.036624,
      "text": "in conservation and was deployed to engender"
    },
    {
      "start": 30.062666,
      "end": 32.510583000000004,
      "text": "support for protecting damaged ecosystems."
    },
    {
      "start": 33.844083,
      "end": 36.005540999999994,
      "text": "Conservation initiatives were mobilized"
    },
    {
      "start": 36.031583,
      "end": 37.815456999999995,
      "text": "where human activities had damaged"
    },
    {
      "start": 37.841499999999996,
      "end": 40.48470699999999,
      "text": "ecosystems, especially by removing vital"
    },
    {
      "start": 40.497749999999996,
      "end": 41.604541,
      "text": "keystone predators."
    },
    {
      "start": 42.952082999999995,
      "end": 45.360957,
      "text": "In addition, wolves often kept animals from"
    },
    {
      "start": 45.38699999999999,
      "end": 46.923457,
      "text": "grazing in riparian areas,"
    },
    {
      "start": 47.20991599999999,
      "end": 49.123999,
      "text": "which protected beavers from having food"
    },
    {
      "start": 49.13699999999999,
      "end": 50.517208,
      "text": "sources encroached upon."
    },
    {
      "start": 51.84408299999999,
      "end": 54.33108199999999,
      "text": "Ecological engineering uses ecology and"
    },
    {
      "start": 54.35712499999999,
      "end": 56.24516599999999,
      "text": "engineering to predict, design,"
    },
    {
      "start": 56.41441599999999,
      "end": 59.005540999999994,
      "text": "construct or restore, and manage ecosystems"
    },
    {
      "start": 59.03158299999999,
      "end": 60.177457999999994,
      "text": "for mutual benefit."
    },
    {
      "start": 61.50408299999999,
      "end": 63.965040999999985,
      "text": "These engineered ecosystems integrate human"
    },
    {
      "start": 63.99108299999999,
      "end": 66.29574899999999,
      "text": "society with its natural environment for the"
    },
    {
      "start": 66.32179099999999,
      "end": 68.61345799999998,
      "text": "benefit of both balanced living systems."
    }
  ],
